caption: GATES Setting Rules — Computer Progression and Effective Complexity
technology-rule: computer-progression-and-effective-complexity

In GATES, computers advance faster after TL9. A Tiny implant computer has base Complexity 3 at TL9, 5 at TL10, 7 at TL11, and 9 at TL12. Fast adds +1 Complexity and multiplies cost by 20. Genius adds +2 Complexity and multiplies cost by 500. Fast and Genius are mutually exclusive. FTL adds +1 Complexity and multiplies cost by 100; it may combine with Fast or Genius, but it is normally TL11^ and is not available early by default.
